@title Tides of Trade
@subtitle Press release: a new exhibition at the Brightwater Maritime Museum

## At a glance
- Opens to the public on November 14, 2026, and closes May 9, 2027
- 140 objects from 12 countries
- Curated by Dr. Rasmus Lindholm

## About the exhibition
"Tides of Trade" follows the spice, tea and cotton routes between 1600 and 1850. Visitors trace them through original ship ledgers, navigation instruments and a full-size reconstruction of a cargo hold. The centerpiece is the 1783 log of the brig Hesper, shown to the public for the first time.

## Visiting
table = Ticket,Price; Adults,$18; Seniors,$14; Children under 12 and museum members,Free

The museum is open Tuesday to Sunday from 10:00 to 17:00, and until 20:00 on Thursdays. The exhibition is fully step-free.

## Programs
- An opening gala on November 13, 2026, at 18:30, with tickets at $120
- A curator talk every first Saturday at 14:00
- Free school visits for groups of up to 40 students, booked at schools@brightwatermuseum.example

